Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.

## Validation at execute time

- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L17)).
- When a caller supplies `null`, an array, or another non-object value, `ToolRegistry.execute` throws a `TypeError` naming the tool and the value's kind rather than exposing the value or treating the caller bug as a model-correctable schema rejection ([validated by: rejects non-object input as a caller bug without exposing its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L30)).
- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L48), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property with its field path and expected type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L87), [validated by: logs a safe validation rejection with its field path and failed constraint](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L102)). Rejection logs name the failing property path and constraint ([validated by: logs a required-property rejection with its field path and constraint](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L123)).
- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input with an extra property through to the executor unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L47)). A rejected enum value is reported with its field path and the `enum` constraint ([validated by: names the enum constraint when an input value is not allowed](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L157)).
- Validation failures identify nested property paths with dot-separated field names ([validated by: names nested property paths with dots in validation failures](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L178)).
- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake. Caller-supplied non-object input is likewise a `TypeError`, because it is a programming error rather than a model-correctable schema rejection.

## Schema compilation and caching

- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L96)).
- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles a static tool schema once across ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L62)).
- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema returned for each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L204)).

## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery

- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L114)).
